# Versioning (SemVer)

Port Harbor uses **Semantic Versioning**: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`.

| Bump | When |
|------|------|
| **MAJOR** | Breaking UX/API change (e.g. remove a menu action, change restart semantics) |
| **MINOR** | New feature, backward compatible (e.g. new framework detection) |
| **PATCH** | Bug fix, docs, internal refactor with no user-facing change |

## Releases

- Ship versions as **annotated git tags**: `v1.2.3` (leading `v` required).
- Tag only from `main` after the release commit is merged.
- Do **not** bump version on every PR — only when cutting a release.
- Keep a root `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog style: Added / Changed / Fixed / Security).
- Unreleased work goes under `## [Unreleased]`; move it into `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` at release time.

```bash
# Example release
git tag -a v0.2.0 -m "v0.2.0"
git push origin v0.2.0
```

## Package / app version

- Do not invent a version field in `Package.swift` for this executable.
- If a macOS bundle/`Info.plist` is added later, keep `CFBundleShortVersionString` in sync with the git tag (without the `v` prefix).
